From b5a55788d705ec6919112cfbe9332125cc1ab4dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: Dolby Vision with the HDMI 1.4b signalling,
 where the display asks and it is on

A TV that asks for the older Dolby Vision signalling, the HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame (2016 LG OLED
among them; CDisplayInfo::SupportsHdmi14bDolbyVision()), gets HDR10 from native output: "legacy",
"older signalling (HDMI 1.4b), not sent". With "Dolby Vision with the older signalling (HDMI
1.4b)" turned on (System > Display, videoscreen.hadesdvhdmi14b, off by default), native output
sends it the tunnel of the Standard mode with that signalling:

- only where the display asks for it, with QS (the rule of the first commit of this series): the
  setting is shown only there (the condition supportsdvhdmi14b, CWinSystemBase::
  SupportsDVHdmi14bChoice()), and is enabled with native output, at the level of the Low-Latency
  one. Whether a TV takes the signal cannot be known from here: the help says so, and that wrong
  colours mean the setting is to be turned off;
- only where the kernel or the module says it can (DVBRIDGE_DV_HDMI14B_LAB; NV_HDMI_DV_HDMI14B,
  nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9045 and nvidia-legacy-open-9058); else the reason is
  "hdmi14bdriver", and no other signal is sent instead;
- the output is captured as for the Standard mode, with that property (CDVBridgeState::Capture(),
  hdmi14b; on nvidia-drm the HDMI 1.4b InfoFrame of the mode, made again with each change of mode);
- the metadata are those of the display management version of its block (version 1: its field;
  version 0: its major version): a display of 2 or 3 is sent the content mapping v2.9 part, as the
  others of those versions;
- 2160p at 50 and 60 Hz by the 2160p60 bit of the block;
- the log says, once per change, that the setting is on, and the verdict of native output names
  the signalling and the setting.

The decision is that of DV_DISPLAY (previous commit): the signal HDMI14B, the reason "legacy" left
out for it, its 2160p60 and display management version; the tuple of what native output depends on
counts the signalling only with the setting on. Strings in English, with es_ES, es_AR and es_MX in
Estuary (core #39878 and #39879, Estuary #31923, #31924 and #31932, used by no other branch).

With the setting off nothing changes for any display. Tested on the host: CDisplayInfo
before this series and of this tree, each built with libdisplay-info 0.4.0 of the build, on the
603 EDIDs of the corpus and 518 600 mutations of them: every answer of the one before the same,
and its log lines; with the setting off, the decisions (reason, signal, QS, 2160p60, display
management version, the support shown, what native output depends on, which settings are read)
those of the code before this series, written in the test as its WinSystemGbm.cpp has them,
with Low-Latency off and on; with it on, exactly the 41 displays of the corpus that ask for the
signalling with QS change (14 of display management 2, 27 of 3, 10 with the 2160p60 bit), from
"legacy" to native output; the setting is offered for those 41. 10 of 10 mutations of DV_DISPLAY
are caught; the .po files are well formed (po_check.py).

Not seen on a display: nobody of the project has a TV that asks for this signalling.
